Two further reduction-loop codegen wins on top of the defer-aware folding:
- emit_avx_binary_256 gains a commutative fast path: when args[1] is the
  last-stored/deferred value (in ymm0) and args[0] is a foldable memory
  operand, emit 'op m0, ymm0, ymm0' with no vmovdqa rename.
- VecLoad* skip materializing a constant-0 offset into rcx (the vectorizer
  passes (array_gep, 0)): 'vmovupd (rax), ymm0' instead of 'xorl ecx,ecx;
  vmovupd (rax,rcx), ymm0'.

F64 sum loop: load+add(acc folded)+store = 3 arithmetic instrs/iter.
Benchmarks (min-of-5, pinned): F64 sum 0.624 vs gcc 0.616; F64 dot 0.250
vs 0.247; F32 dot 0.124 vs 0.246 (2x). Regression 126/126, correctness
50/50, intrinsics 3/3.
